From: Ondřej Tůma <mcbig@zeropage.cz>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: Do not crash on startup when python3-pynvim is not installed

formiko/__main__.py always tries gi.require_version("Vte", "3.91"),
which succeeds whenever the gir1.2-vte-3.91 typelib is installed (a
Recommends of the formiko package, so installed by default). Because
document_page.py only checked gi.get_required_version("Vte") before
importing formiko.vim, and formiko.vim imports pynvim unconditionally,
formiko fails to start with "ModuleNotFoundError: No module named
'pynvim'" on any system that has the formiko package installed
without formiko-vim (which is the only package depending on
python3-pynvim since the formiko-vim split).

Catch the missing-pynvim case and treat Vim editor support as simply
unavailable, the same way it already behaves when Vte itself is
missing.

Bug: https://github.com/ondratu/formiko/issues/32
Origin: backport, https://github.com/ondratu/formiko/commit/7ac2d9dc203ad60f796cb9c97efec6da51bee37b
Forwarded: not-needed
---
 formiko/document_page.py | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/formiko/document_page.py b/formiko/document_page.py
index c0e3e76..6eaf78e 100644
--- a/formiko/document_page.py
+++ b/formiko/document_page.py
@@ -18,7 +18,12 @@ from formiko.user import UserPreferences, View
 from formiko.widgets import ImutableDict

 if get_required_version("Vte"):
-    from formiko.vim import VimEditor
+    try:
+        from formiko.vim import VimEditor
+    except ModuleNotFoundError as error:
+        if error.name != "pynvim":
+            raise
+        VimEditor = None

 RE_WORD = re.compile(r"([\w]+)", re.U)
 RE_CHAR = re.compile(r'[\w \t\.,\?\(\)"\']', re.U)
